{
	"$comment": "The scenarios for `agentic.chat.ask`, and the only statement of the contract the chat driver is held to. `Crate/ChatDriver/Test/Parity.rs` reads this file and `generated/chat-driver.timing.json`, drives the port through a scripted page, and asserts each case's `expect` block. `effects` is the ordered list of what the fake page observed - the protocol the implementation spoke - so a port that returns the right value by the wrong route fails. Trace and source objects are written with their keys in alphabetical order, which is the order `serde_json`'s map serialises, so the file reads the way the port reports. A case's `rust` names the unit case in `Crate/ChatDriver/Test/Chat.rs` that proves it; a case whose rule only the fake can express says so in `scenario-only`; and `Parity.rs` refuses a case that names a test which does not exist. `Documentation/Parity.md` says what this file establishes and what it does not.",
